  "_comment": [
    "Shared boundary table for the NFL-week resolver twins:",
    "  scripts/nfl_week.py   <- scripts/tests/test_nfl_week.py",
    "  web/lib/nfl-week.ts   <- web/__tests__/lib/nfl-week.test.ts",
    "Both suites read THIS file, so the Python and TypeScript implementations",
    "cannot drift apart without one of them going red.",
    "",
    "regular_season_start is the Thursday of Week 1 (2026-09-10, the Thursday",
    "after Labor Day). The week boundary is the Tuesday two days earlier,",
    "2026-09-08, so Monday-night games stay in their own week and the slate",
    "flips on Tuesday morning.",
    "",
    "season_cases exercise resolve_window / resolveWindow against a MULTI-SEASON",
    "calendar. The NFL season is taken from which kickoff we sit between, not",
    "from the active league-calendar row: Ottoneu rolls its league season in",
    "early January while NFL Week 18 is played a day or two later."
  ],
